abstract: >-
  Code, data and stored outputs for the computation note "A numerical audit of factor-based FPTP seat
  distributions: a Great Britain 2024 case study" (draft v0.2.2, not peer reviewed). Given common factors, seat
  totals are computed with the Poisson-binomial recursion and convolution across regions; the factor integral is
  done by a hybrid of scrambled Sobol points and regional Gauss-Hermite rules. The note reports how the usual
  scramble error bar missed a regional-rule bias (Green) and an under-resolved rare outer contribution (Other),
  and how each was located by a different computation path. The model is a fixed computational case, not a
  forecasting product. Code under MIT; the note and stored outputs under CC BY 4.0; data under their sources'
  terms (DATA_LICENSES.md). Developed with extensive assistance from Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) and reviewed
  with GPT 6.1 Sol (OpenAI); the author directed and reviewed the work and is responsible for the content.
keywords:
  - first-past-the-post
  - seat distribution
  - Poisson-binomial
  - randomized quasi-Monte Carlo
  - numerical audit
  - UK general election 2024
